# Mac: Support Apple silicon mac for running native windows on arm softwares.
# https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/11638 state=opened
# ntdll: Support running on Apple Silicon macOS.
The kernel on Apple Silicon enforces a default 4GB page zero for
executables and rejects smaller ones at exec time, so the loader is
built as a standard PIE executable instead of a dlopen-style image
(no fixed load address, following the OS ASLR policy).
The 0x7ffe0000 address it not accessible so we need to use dynamic
KUSER_SHARED_DATA instead. It is actually redundant since windows
does store the KUSER_SHARED_DATA in special register.
KUSER_SHARED_DATA = TPIDRRO_EL0 - 0x1000;

Apple silicon uses 16k page, and wine has commits to compile
wine with 64k section alignment, which is correct.

Also x18 register can still be accessed before macos 12. After
that we cannot. so we force wine to be compiled with macos12 to
bypass kernel restriction
